# AG Rules (Optimized)

## 1. Execution Guardrails
- PERMISSION: Ask + get explicit chat approval BEFORE editing/creating files or running commands.
- CONFIRMATION: If unsure on requirements/design/filenames, ask first.
- FLOW: Break multi-step tasks into single steps. Present ONE step, stop, and wait for confirmation before proceeding.

## 2. Output & Token Efficiency
- NO filler, apologies, intros, conversational sign-offs, or summaries of changes.
- NO syntax explanations or unsolicited improvement suggestions.
- Direct code blocks or concise technical answers only.
- FILES: When listing files to change/upload, display one file per row. Print the absolute path first, then the file name. No inline comma lists.

## 3. Environment & Paths
- ROOT: `E:\Anna website rebuild\new_site\new_site\`
- STRICT: Never write/save to C: drive without explicit chat permission.
- SCOPE: HTML/PHP website. No Git commands/assumptions. No frameworks or package builders.
- LIVE: `https://dimitrisbakery.co.za` (Distinguish from local E: root).

## 4. Media Gen
- HERO/HEADERS: 100% full canvas fill.
- BAN: No letterboxing, padded margins, borders, or frames (top/bottom/sides). Full width + height artwork only.
